  "nl_text": "This database schema, named rschema_0450, is used to store information about a company's assets, users, and asset circulation records. It consists of five tables: department, user, asset_category, asset, and circulation_record.\nThe department table stores information about the different departments within the company, including their department ID, name, and description. The user table stores information about the users who have access to the assets, including their user ID, name, and affiliated department.\nThe asset_category table stores information about the different types of assets, including their type ID, category name, and description. The asset table stores information about the assets themselves, including their asset ID, name, type, affiliated department, status, scrapping indicator, creator, creation time, updater, and update time.\nThe circulation_record table stores information about the circulation of assets, including the asset ID, the user ID of the user who is circulating the asset, the circulation status, and the circulation time.\nThe schema enforces domain integrity by specifying the data types for each column and whether they allow null values. It also enforces entity integrity by defining primary keys and unique constraints for each table. Referential integrity is enforced by defining foreign keys that reference other tables, with update and delete rules that cascade or restrict changes to the referenced tables. Finally, the schema includes indexes and constraints to optimize query performance and ensure data consistency.",
  "gold_question": "Asset Management System Design for a Company is as follows:\nThe company has multiple departments, with department information including Department ID, name, and description.\nEach department has multiple users, with user information including User ID, name, and affiliated department.\nThe company manages assets by categories, with asset category information including Type ID, category name, and description.\nAsset information includes Asset ID, name, type, affiliated department, status (such as \"idle\", \"in use\", \"returning\", \"scrapped\"), and scrapping indicator, etc.\nThe asset circulation record includes Asset ID, circulating User ID, circulation status (such as \"pending receipt\", \"received\", \"allocating\", \"allocated\"), etc.\nThe system needs to record the creation and update information of assets, including creator and creation time, updater and update time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0450.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0450\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `asset_category` (\n  `type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`type_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `asset` (\n  `asset_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `scrapping_indicator` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `creator` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updater` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`asset_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `asset_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`type_id`) REFERENCES `asset_category` (`type_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `asset_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `circulation_record` (\n  `record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `asset_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `circulation_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `circulation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `circulation_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`asset_id`) REFERENCES `asset` (`asset_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `circulation_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
